WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:08.120
So there were sadly suspicions that there
may have been police officers who either stood

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:14.380
aside or even helped the Trump rioters on
January 6th.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.270
And sadly, it appears that this is true.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.490
We've now learned that several members of
the United States Capitol Police have been

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:27.680
suspended, according to Acting Capitol Police
Chief Yogananda Pitmen.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.520
Earlier yesterday, Congressman Tim Ryan, a
former guest on this program, said that two

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.020
officers had been suspended.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.820
One officer took a selfie with one of the
violent insurrectionists.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:44.820
Another gave them a tour of the Capitol building,
according to Congressman Ryan.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:51.730
Tim Ryan also saying that there are 10 to
15 ongoing investigations into officer conduct

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.600
during the insurrection.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.969
This was at a press conference given yesterday
by Tim Ryan.

00:00:56.969 --> 00:01:01.710
Ryan also indicated that a third individual
has been arrested, but said it's not currently

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.959
clear if they're a member of the Capitol Police
or the National Guard.

00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:12.390
And this is I mean, listen, there's a few
different things that have to be talked about

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.600
here, first of all.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:23.219
We were cautious when the theories started
that this was a plot and that Capitol Police

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:30.820
in advance were planning to usher in protesters,
and I said as those theories started to be

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.289
presented, let's be careful about that, because
we don't have evidence of that yet.

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:42.599
When we saw, you know, a 15 second video of
police clearing some barricades and that was

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:46.369
pointed to as evidence of a conspiracy involving
the Capitol Police.

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:53.159
I said we have to be careful because anybody
who knows about crowd control knows that once

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:59.639
you know, you are overwhelmed and your physical
barriers will not hold, you do move the physical

00:01:59.639 --> 00:02:04.959
barriers to avoid others and yourself getting
hurt and trampled by the barriers themselves.

00:02:04.959 --> 00:02:06.899
And so I urged caution.

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:08.390
And indeed, what we know.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:14.769
Listen, I think one of the important things
is if your view on police is radically different

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:20.280
today than it was around the George Floyd
protests, then you should question whether

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.360
your view is tuned to reality during the George
Floyd protests.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:30.240
My view was that based on everything I knew,
most police officers are doing their jobs

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.160
to the best of their abilities.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.620
And most police officers are becoming officers,
generally speaking, for the right reasons,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.819
because they want to protect their communities,
do do do something that's good for their communities.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:51.140
And there are a lot there are too many bad
actors that slip through the cracks due to

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.209
lack of systems that prevent them from doing
so.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:58.450
And so when you're talking about an apparatus
as large as law enforcement, there's no doubt

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:04.799
that there will be horrible people in a group
and a bad apple can spoil the bunch.

00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:11.909
So it's not a surprise that now we are starting
to see two, three people suspended, a dozen

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:13.069
under investigation.

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:19.469
I'm sure that there are more than two officers
involved last week and potentially even even

00:03:19.469 --> 00:03:20.859
military folks as well.

00:03:20.859 --> 00:03:22.680
The investigations are ongoing.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.390
That behaved absolutely atrociously.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.049
Eventually there should be firings and not
suspensions.

00:03:30.049 --> 00:03:35.470
But I think it's also important that, you
know, when we jump into the conspiracy theories

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:40.209
or when we start making the claims that aren't
based, in fact, we become just as bad as them

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:41.480
and there's no reason to do it.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.620
Eventually the truth is going to going to
come out.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.260
The suspensions are happening.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.290
The arrests of the rioters are happening,
and it's all happening.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:55.329
And remember, there are also people in law
enforcement who acted heroically last week.

00:03:55.329 --> 00:04:01.420
Eugene Goodman is a Capitol Police officer
who is rightly being hailed as a hero, who

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.970
realized what was going on, realized that
the armed that the violent insurrection, some

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:10.640
of whom we suspect were armed, were getting
into the direction of the Senate chamber in

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.030
which there were senators.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:16.479
And Eugene Goodman lured these rioters in
the opposite direction.

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:19.289
Eugene Goodman made himself a decoy.

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:23.349
So let's take this a step at a time.

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:24.349
Yes.

00:04:24.349 --> 00:04:25.349
Investigations.

00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:29.690
Is anyone surprised that some when you look
at the percentage of of law enforcement that

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.710
voted Trump?

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:37.539
Of course, in that there are going to be some
people that are carried away by what they

00:04:37.539 --> 00:04:41.810
love to see, there were people in law enforcement
who loved what happened last week.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.660
Some even participated off duty.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.720
So, of course, we're seeing this.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.889
So the investigations must continue.

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:52.080
We need attention to be devoted to investigating
supervisors and leadership to figure out what

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.080
happened.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:58.260
And that means both supervisors and leadership
who ignored the signs that were there that

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:02.300
this was likely or probable to happen.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.900
And that needs to be investigated as well.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:09.389
The difficult part is that for every two that
actually helped in a way that warrants a suspension

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:13.610
like the two that have been suspended so far,
there were a bunch that sort of were OK with

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.810
it and kind of look the other way.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.479
And it wasn't criminally negligent, but it's
still very problematic and that is much more

00:05:20.479 --> 00:05:23.210
difficult to weed out and to deal with.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.050
But again, most of the people on duty were
just doing their jobs and they effectively

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.150
ended up abandoned by management and colleagues.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:34.730
Anyone that watches the videos can tell that
a vast majority of the police on scene were

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:40.199
doing their jobs and they were putting themselves
in harm's way and very importantly.

00:05:40.199 --> 00:05:47.110
Any officer that was involved in any way must
be fired, they must lose pension progress

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.889
that they've made and it must be taken extraordinarily
seriously, you're not going to change political

00:05:51.889 --> 00:05:52.910
views by doing this.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:58.379
I understand that if you're a trumpet's, then
you get fired because of your role in the

00:05:58.379 --> 00:05:59.379
riots.

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:00.819
Trump is a police officer.

00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:02.229
You don't all of a sudden become a progressive.

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:04.820
I understand that it would be naive to think
so.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.669
But the point is, much like the point I made
about the need to find an arrest and charge

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:13.940
and throw the book at the rioters themselves,
which is that and we're going to talk momentarily

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:18.180
about the risk of more of these riots coming
up in the next week, eight days.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:23.259
If the punishments aren't severe, they will
be encouraged to do it again.

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:24.340
And that's the biggest risk.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:07:31.319
And it seems that it is sadly 

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:36.030
going to happen.

